  "body": "[PEP 675](https://peps.python.org/pep-0675/) proposes a new `typing.LiteralString` type. The idea is that typecheckers should check that a `LiteralString` is composed only from string literals (i.e. cannot contain user-provided data), to help mitigate e.g. SQL injection attacks. This sounds like a nice-to-have for us, though it's probably not worth picking up until mypy has support for the type (python/mypy#12554).",
